---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Privacy policy';
const description = 'What the Registry Stack Marketplace collects, why, and how to control optional tracking.';
const sharedTrackingEnabled = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SHARED_TRACKING_ENABLED === 'true';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} screen="privacy">
  <section class="mp-wrap mp-section" aria-labelledby="marketplace-privacy-title">
    <p class="mp-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 id="marketplace-privacy-title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <div class="mp-panel-intro">
      <p>
        This policy covers marketplace.registrystack.org. Registry Stack is published by Aubex
        Consulting LLC, 28 Geary St, Ste 650 #189, San Francisco, CA 94108, United States.
      </p>

      <h2>Marketplace use</h2>
      <p>
        You can browse the public catalogue without an account. Packs are not public downloads.
        If you use a pack request form, we collect your email address and any organization, role,
        or request details you choose to provide. We also record the public pack identifier, source
        page, and time of the request in our self-hosted Mautic form system so our team can review
        the request and reply manually. The marketplace never sends a browser tracking identifier
        with this request, even if you accepted optional visit tracking. Submitting a request does
        not sign you up for marketing. If the form is unavailable, you can use the email fallback;
        we then receive your address and message as ordinary business correspondence.
      </p>
      <p>
        The marketplace does not receive the terms you enter in its local catalogue search.
        A contribution form prepares a GitHub
        draft for you to review; it does not submit the draft to Registry Stack automatically.
        GitHub processes information only when you choose to continue there.
      </p>

      <h2>Aggregate analytics</h2>
      <p>
        When configured for publication, the marketplace uses self-hosted, cookie-free Umami
        analytics to count page views and a fixed allowlist of actions, such as a Download pack
        click, a confirmed request, Studio instructions, and opening a contribution draft. Action
        records can contain the public pack identifier and a sanitized marketplace path. They
        never contain search terms, query parameters, form contents, email addresses, or request
        tokens. Umami analytics are separate from the request form and the optional Mautic visit
        tracking described below; they are not connected to a name or email.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional visit tracking</h2>
      {!sharedTrackingEnabled && <p>Optional visit tracking is currently disabled on this marketplace. The following controls apply when it is enabled.</p>}
      <p>
        Optional Mautic tracking relies on your consent. A fresh acceptance covers the main Registry
        Stack website, its canonical documentation, and this marketplace for six months. An earlier
        choice covering only the website and documentation does not authorize marketplace tracking.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before acceptance, the marketplace does not ask the shared bridge to send a Mautic page
        view. After acceptance, it sends only the canonical public route, fixed public page title,
        and referring site's origin. It sends no query, fragment, search value, contribution text,
        email address, or browser identifier. The identifier remains inside the bridge on
        registrystack.org; the marketplace cannot request it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use <strong>Tracking preferences</strong> to reject or withdraw consent. Withdrawal stops
        future optional tracking across all three properties and clears the bridge's browser
        identifier. It does not automatically delete records already received. Registry Stack also
        treats Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control as requests to keep optional tracking off.
        If the bridge, storage, or tracker is blocked, optional tracking stays off and the public
        catalogue remains available.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and linked services</h2>
      <p>
        GitHub Pages hosts this static site and processes ordinary server-log data to deliver and
        protect it. Source links and contribution drafts can lead to GitHub, which has
        its own privacy practices. The main website and Registry Docs publish their own notices for
        processing other than the shared optional tracking choice.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to access, correct, or delete personal data through the
        <a href="https://registrystack.org/contact/?type=privacy">Registry Stack privacy contact form</a>.
        Request details and related correspondence are retained as ordinary business records while
        they remain relevant. Aggregate analytics may not identify records that belong to a
        particular visitor.
      </p>

      <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> November 4, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
